# The function and a class below it are handed out, so `this` is only expected, and objects of both layouts are in use. Behind `new.target === Base` no object of an heir arrives: the guess asks for the shape of Base's own layout alone. It stays a guess: the test is built. On the other side of the test of new.target both are asked for. Without guards of parameters, which would test `this` at the entry. f2 = Base, L0 = its layout, L1 = Below.
# RUN: walk f2 mechanisms=all-ParameterGuards
# CHECK: = ShapeTest v0 layouts=[L0] 
# CHECK: = ShapeTest v0 layouts=[L0, L1] 
# -- source: this-behind-a-test-that-new-target-is-the-function-itself-is-asked-for-its-own-shape-alone.js
